From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: give the IOMMUs the VE's MBUS port gates

Name each video engine master's MBUS matrix port gate as a "masterN" clock
of the IOMMU that serves it, so that `iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver` (revision of 2026-09-24)
holds the gate while the master translates. A master's register block
inside the IOMMU does not answer while its port is gated; the access
stalls the bus.

  iommu1  master0, master1  CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC   MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING bit 14
          (VE_MBUS0, VE_MBUS1 -- the decoder's two masters, one port gate)
  iommu0  master3           CLK_MBUS_VE_ENC0  MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING bit 12
          (VE_ENC)

  Source  the master indices: UM V1.00 ch. 10 and `arm64-dts-a733-the-two-iommus`'s table (four and
          six master blocks read on silicon). The gate per master: measured on the
          8 GB board, 2026-09-22 -- with the VE released, the per-master
          range invalidation (+0x054) of IOMMU1 completes with bit 14 set
          alone and times out with every other decoder clock, gate and
          reset set alone; for IOMMU0 the same with bit 12. Decoder held
          alone: IOMMU1 clears, IOMMU0 times out; encoder alone: the
          reverse.
  Ids     CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC 108, CLK_MBUS_VE_ENC0 107, from `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-ve-plls-module-clocks-gates-and-resets`, which is
          why this is not in `arm64-dts-a733-the-two-iommus`: the ids do not exist yet at `arm64-dts-a733-the-two-iommus`.

DE0 (iommu1 master 2) gets no entry: its port (bit 11, DESYS) read 1 in
every state measured, display off included. The other masters
(USB, CSI, ISP, DI, G2D, EINK) have no consumer and no measured gate.

No consumer lists `iommus` for a VE master on this tree, so nothing
changes at runtime: `iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver` enables a master clock only for a master with a
user. The clocks become active as soon as a VE node lists `iommus` (for example
in a test DTB).

VERIFIED: applies at fuzz 0 on main after `arm64-dts-a733-cpu-opp-clock-latency-measured`; the dtb builds, and the
decompiled dtb carries clock-names "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus",
"master3" on iommu@3900000 and "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus", "master0",
"master1" on iommu@3910000; CHECK_DTBS against `iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver`'s binding reports
nothing for either node.

HARDWARE-PROVEN on the 8 GB board, 2026-09-24 (6.18.36-t407 and 6.18.53-t407,
with a test script): with the VE behind the IOMMUs, bits 12
and 14 stay set while both engines are runtime-suspended (VE_BGR_REG 0:
resets asserted, bus gates masked) and 1001 IOMMU1 unmaps complete; the
same kernel with these clocks removed from the dtb stalls the bus on the
first unmap, like the kernel before `iommu-sun60i-add-the-allwinner-a733-iommu-driver`'s revision. On the product dtb
the gates follow the engines, and the idle draw is the same either way
(3.711 against 3.709 W, 0.1 W resolution).

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -1138,8 +1138,15 @@ iommu0: iommu@3900000 {
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_IOMMU0_SYS_MCLK>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU0_SYS_PCLK>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU0_SYS_HCLK>,
-				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU0>;
-			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus";
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU0>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_ENC0>;
+			/*
+			 * master3: VE_ENC's MBUS matrix port gate
+			 * (MBUS_MAT_CLK_GATING bit 12). Its master block does
+			 * not answer while the port is gated; the driver holds
+			 * the gate while the master translates.
+			 */
+			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus", "master3";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU0>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 		};
@@ -1151,8 +1158,18 @@ iommu1: iommu@3910000 {
 			clocks = <&ccu CLK_IOMMU1_SYS_MCLK>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU1_SYS_PCLK>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_IOMMU1_SYS_HCLK>,
-				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>;
-			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus";
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_IOMMU1>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC>,
+				 <&ccu CLK_MBUS_VE_DEC>;
+			/*
+			 * master0/master1: VE_MBUS0/VE_MBUS1, both behind the
+			 * decoder's one MBUS matrix port gate (bit 14), measured
+			 * as the one bit that lets their invalidation complete.
+			 * DE0 (master2) has no entry: its port (bit 11,
+			 * DESYS) read 1 in every state measured.
+			 */
+			clock-names = "mclk", "pclk", "hclk", "mbus",
+				      "master0", "master1";
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_IOMMU1>;
 			#iommu-cells = <1>;
 		};
